# EAS Build archive excludes.
# Why this exists: 71 agent worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ (8.6GB, each with
# its own node_modules) pushed the archive 228MB -> 1.2GB and the upload 400'd.
# KEEP THIS CONSERVATIVE. A previous version globbed *.png and stripped the app
# icon/splash assets, which failed the Bundle JavaScript phase. Exclude only
# directories that cannot contribute to the app bundle.
#
# ANCHOR EVERY ROOT-LEVEL ENTRY WITH A LEADING SLASH. This file uses gitignore
# semantics, so a bare `screens/` matches a directory named `screens` at ANY
# depth — including `mobile/src/screens/`, i.e. every screen in the app. That
# is exactly what happened: builds 99 and 100 (v1.12.1) both died at Bundle
# JavaScript with "Unable to resolve module ../screens/SignInScreen", while
# `npx expo export` succeeded locally, because the failure only exists inside
# the archive. Second instance of this bug class in this file.
/.claude/worktrees/
/archive/
/staged-work/
/feedback-workspace/
/mockups/
/screens/
mobile/ios/build/
#
# LOCAL-ONLY FILES. Once this file exists, eas-cli stops reading every
# .gitignore ("if .easignore exists, .gitignore files are not used", eas-cli
# vcs/local.js) and copies the working tree into the archive, so anything
# gitignored but not listed here is uploaded to EAS. `eas build:inspect --stage
# archive` proved it on 2026-10-15 for secrets.local.env, data/*.db, .env files,
# signing files and the qa scratch DBs. Every secret, credential, DB and env
# pattern from any .gitignore is repeated below; mobile/tests/check-easignore.js
# fails CI when one goes missing. These file globs stay unanchored, like their
# .gitignore originals, so they match at any depth. Unlike the bare directory
# names warned about above, they can't collide with app source.
secrets.local.env*
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.xcode.env.local
*.db
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
/data/
/qa/sim-runs/
/qa/**/scratch*/
